{ You have just played a6. This time he answers with a second pawn in the middle. }
5. c4 { Two pawns side by side, squeezing you. This is the bind. How do you start? [%csl Rd5] } 5... Nf6 { Right. Poke the e pawn first, before anything else. [%cal Gf6e4] } (5... Bb4+ { A check, but he blocks and his knight lands on a fine square. } 6. Nd2 Ne7 7. Nc2 { You spent a move and he improved. }) (5... b6 { Slow. He gets to build the whole clamp in peace. } 6. f3 Nf6 7. Nc3 { Now the pawns are set and you never poked them. }) (5... Qc7 { The queen looks nice there, but the middle is the emergency. } 6. Nc3 Nf6 7. a3 { He is comfortable and you are still cramped. }) (5... Nc6 { Trading knights helps him: it fills the middle with his pawn. } 6. Nc3 Qc7 7. Be3 { The bind gets stronger, not weaker. }) 6. Nc3 { He guards the pawn with the knight. Now pin that knight to something. } 6... Bb4 { The bishop pins the knight, so the e pawn is not really guarded. [%cal Gb4c3,Gf6e4] } (6... d5 { The right break at the wrong moment. He just takes twice. } 7. cxd5 exd5 8. exd5 { A pawn down for nothing. Pin first. }) (6... Qc7 { Quiet, and the clamp stays. } 7. a3 b6 8. Be3 { He shuts the door and you never got the break in. }) (6... d6 { Solid, and now the break is much harder to get. } 7. Be2 Be7 8. g4 { He grabs space on the wing as well. }) (6... Qa5 { The queen pins from far away, but she gets chased. } 7. Bd3 Nc6 8. Nb3 { She has to run and he gained time. }) 7. Qd3 { The queen props the pawn up. Now the break, right now. } 7... d5 { There it is. The bind cracks open before he is ready. [%cal Gd5e4,Gd5c4] } (7... d6 { One square short, and the moment is gone. } 8. Nc2 Bxc3+ 9. Qxc3 { He untangles and the clamp holds. }) (7... O-O { Safe, but he closes the door with the pawn. } 8. e5 Ne8 9. Be2 { Your knight is pushed to the edge and the break is dead. }) (7... Nc6 { Trading into his pawn again. } 8. Nxc6 dxc6 9. Qxd8+ { The queens come off and he is just better. }) 8. exd5 { He takes. Take back with the pawn, keeping the middle full. } 8... exd5 { Beautiful. His clamp is gone and your pieces breathe. [%csl Gd5] } (8... O-O { The pawn is hanging! He simply keeps it. } 9. dxe6 fxe6 10. Bg5 { A clean pawn down and your king side is torn. }) (8... Nbd7 { Slow, and the pawn on d5 walks away. } 9. Nc2 Nc5 10. Qd4 { You are a pawn light with nothing to show. }) (8... Bxc3+ { Trading first only helps him rebuild. } 9. bxc3 O-O 10. dxe6 { And the pawn is gone as well. }) 9. Be2 { He develops quietly. Finish the job: get your king safe. } 9... O-O (9... Nc6 { Also completely fine. } 10. cxd5 Nxd5 11. Nxc6 { Equal and lively. Castling first is tidier. }) (9... dxc4 { Handing him the middle back for one pawn. } 10. Qxc4 Bxc3+ 11. Qxc3 { His queen sits in the middle and you have no attack. }) (9... h6 { A wasted breath while your king waits. } 10. Qe3+ Be7 11. cxd5 { A check first, and the pawn goes. }) 0-1


