{ No help this time. You have played a6 and he brings the bishop out. Play our line. }
5. Bd3 { Do you remember where the dark bishop belongs? } 5... Bc5 { That is the one. It leans on his knight and looks through to f2. [%cal Gc5d4,Gc5f2] } (5... Nf6 { Playable, but the bishop was the piece with the job. } 6. O-O d6 7. c4 { He takes the space while you develop quietly. }) (5... Qc7 { A fine Sicilian square, and not our move order. } 6. O-O b6 7. Re1 { Sound. The bishop comes first in our line. }) (5... Ne7 { Also good, heading for g6. } 6. O-O Nbc6 7. c3 { Fine chess, but recall the bishop move. }) (5... Be7 { Too modest. Think about which diagonal bites. } 6. O-O d6 7. c4 { He builds in comfort. }) 6. Nb3 { He asks your bishop a question. Where does it go, and why? } 6... Ba7 { Into the corner, where no piece can ever come and trade it off. [%csl Ga7] } (6... Be7 { Safe, but you have given up the whole diagonal. } 7. Qg4 g6 8. O-O { He gets a free poke at your king side. }) (6... Bb6 { So close. One square further is the untouchable one. } 7. Nc3 d6 8. Bd2 { His pieces can still come and bother it. }) (6... Bb4+ { A check for its own sake. Count what it costs. } 7. Nc3 Nc6 8. Qg4 { Your g pawn is hanging now. }) (6... Bf8 { All the way back. Two moves for nothing. } 7. c4 Nc6 8. Nc3 { He built the clamp while you shuffled. }) 7. Qe2 { The queen comes to e2. Now a small pawn move that frees a big piece. } 7... d6 (7... Ne7 { The engine's pick, and genuinely good. } 8. Be3 O-O 9. Nc3 { Sound. Ours opens the light bishop first. }) (7... Nc6 { Also good. } 8. Be3 Nge7 9. Nc3 { Fine, but recall the pawn move. }) (7... e5 { It grabs room but leaves a hole he will love. } 8. Be3 Bxe3 9. Qxe3 { A knight lands on d5 and never leaves. }) (7... Qc7 { The lady walks out too early. } 8. Qg4 Kf8 9. Qe2 { Your king cannot castle now. }) 8. O-O { His king is away. Which of your pieces is still at home? } 8... Nf6 (8... Nc6 { Just as good, and we play the other one first. } 9. Be3 Nf6 10. c4 { The same house by another door. }) (8... Bd7 { Quiet and sound. } 9. Be3 Bxe3 10. Qxe3 { Fine, but a knight was in more of a hurry. }) (8... e5 { Too soon again. The hole on d5 opens first. } 9. Be3 Bxe3 10. Qxe3 { He aims straight at d5. }) (8... Nd7 { The wrong knight, and it shuts your bishop in. } 9. c4 Ngf6 10. Nc3 { The other one belonged there. }) 9. c4 { He clamps the middle with a second pawn. Do you let him have it? } 9... e5 { Never. The pawn steps up and the middle is shared. That is the whole line. [%csl Gd4,Ge5] } (9... O-O { Good and safe, and the engine is happy with it. } 10. Be3 Bb6 11. Nc3 { Also fine. Ours stakes the middle at once. }) (9... Nc6 { Every bit as good. } 10. Be3 O-O 11. Nc3 { Sound. The pawn push is our idea. }) (9... Nbd7 { Fine, heading for the e5 square with a knight. } 10. Nc3 Ne5 11. Be3 { Also good, just slower. }) (9... Qc7 { Playable, and it does nothing about the clamp. } 10. Nc3 Nbd7 11. Be3 { He is comfortable and you still must push. }) 0-1
